{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ marius roman military reforms recruitment)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_165839757#7_326728357","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1870","rank":3,"snippet":"Similarities Between The Inca And The Aztecs Incas And Aztec Culture Oppression Of Women In Aunt Jennifer´s Tiger's By Adrienne Rich Compare And Contrast Inca And Aztec Empires California Race And Class China And Rome Dbq Analysis Mexican Revolution Vs Russian Revolution Essay \" , \"segment\": \"The Incas used their military positions to control neighboring land, and they would take hostages from neighboring ruling classes in order to achieve obedience and to brainwash them with Inca governing beliefs. Therefore, the <cover>military used well built roads… Read More Words: 1041 - Pages: 5 Reforms By Gaius Marius: The Decline Of The Late Roman Republic There was a major recruitment </cover>problem which came from public land being bought off by powerful groups from the senate around 180 BC to 170 BC. They used this land to produce cash crops from farm slaves. Being a part of the military was more of a privilege than anything. Only certain people could enlist and battle arms was not provided, but land rewards made people have a will to fight anyway. Marius died in 86 BC, he still yet scrambled for power.… Read More Words:\" , \"start_char\"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_241157139#7_545155934","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_241157139#8_545157995","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
