{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"marius reforms\" landless army)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#10_784197829","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1876","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#10_784197829\" , \"end_char\": 8067.000000 , \"headings\": \"Impact of Gaius Marius’ Reforms Impact of Gaius <cover>Marius’ Reforms Get Help With Your Essay Rationale: Interest: Inquiry: Choice: Sources: Cite This Work DMCA / Removal Request \" , \"segment\": \"Consequently, the landless troops who had nowhere to live after serving posed a dangerous precedent for the Roman hierarchy as senators had to offer retirement benefits like grants of land from newly conquered areas (White, 2011). After these reforms were introduced, the Germanic and Celtic tribes were crushed by the revolutionised Roman army. </cover>Marius fought for his soldier’s rights and persuaded the Senate to grant land to the retiring veterans. This one reform that impacted the lives of many Romans outside of serving in the army, ended up contributing significantly to the decline of the Republic (Daily History, 2019). There were many repercussions behind this reform which were politically problematic as it gave too much control and power to the Plebeian classes and further plagued the Republic until its inevitable collapse in 30 BCE (About ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#9_784196069","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
