{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1859"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2408228940#7_3193919492","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1859","rank":14,"snippet":"of the Romans after the Punic Wars, you also have to bear in mind Marius’s reforms. During the early Republic and up to the Punic Wars, only full citizens, owning a house and lands, could participate in the army campaigns. They were required to be citizens with lands because they had to pay for their own equipment and sustenance. After the famous Batle of Cannae, where between 50 and 75 thousand <cover>Roman legionnaires were killed, Rome found itself in a highly vulnerable position, for it was very hard to find as many citizens to replenish the ranks of the army. Because o Continue Reading Besides the high birth rate of the Romans after the Punic Wars, you also have to bear in mind Marius’s reforms. </cover>During the early Republic and up to the Punic Wars, only full citizens, owning a house and lands, could participate in the army campaigns. They were required to be citizens with lands because they had to pay for their own equipment and sustenance. After the famous Batle of Cannae, where between 50 and 75 thousand Roman legionnaires were killed, Rome found itself in a highly vulnerable position, for it was very hard to ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_378001354#7_784192484","rank":13,"relevance":3}]}}
